/**
@page redmine_plugin Redmine plugin boundaries

The plugin is Ruby on Rails integration; Doxygen does not natively parse Ruby.
This page maps its boundaries without claiming generated Ruby API coverage.

@section redmine_entry Entry and authorization
`plugins/redmine_esa/config/routes.rb` declares browser and service routes.
`init.rb` declares View ESA, Submit ESA and Review ESA permissions.
`app/controllers/esa_controller.rb` derives visible project/ticket scopes from
the logged-in user, excludes private issues and calls ESA from the server.
Browser requests never receive the ESA service token.

@section redmine_forward Forwarding and local metadata
`lib/esa/payload.rb` builds the issue snapshot. A human forwarding action creates
an `EsaEvent` durable outbox entry with actor/time; the Go service acknowledges it
after persistence. Creation, editing, import and metadata saves do not forward.
`EsaTicketSource` stores one local metadata record per issue. Saving updates that
record; each forwarding captures a separate immutable input.

@section redmine_ui Status, report and form filling
`lib/esa/presentation.rb` is the read-only UI projection. The ticket page uses
`assets/javascripts/ticket.js` to poll status without replacing unsaved form
values. Extensionless status/suggestion URLs use the Redmine session and an
Accept JSON header. A separate report page contains findings and review forms.
Filling metadata is reversible and does not save, forward or approve anything.

@section redmine_storage State authority
The plugin stores no ESA state. ESA keeps it in a JSON file or in its own
Postgres database; the former Redmine state API was removed, and plugin
migration `005_drop_esa_state_records.rb` drops its tables.
*/
